  },
  RehomedBinWetRow {
    entry: "dag/test/claim/dag_compile_clean_shard_totality_witness_test.dag",
    function: "compile_clean_shard_totality_holds_on_live_tree",
    reason: "Class C corpus-totality claim (docs/plans/test-decomposition-wcf-cut.md §5, criterion 2, session bright-newt-31 2026-07-25): shells out git.Inspect.Toplevel + shell.Find.Files over the whole live tree to prove the shard roster is total against the real corpus (~15s) — the claim is legitimately corpus-grain, not shrinkable, since the whole point is whether the REAL tree's partition is still total. The mechanism (orphan/duplicate/surplus verdict algebra) is proven per-PR on synthetic glob results by compile_clean_shard_totality_algebra_holds, which stays per-PR",
