fn falsifier_rehomed_bin_wet_entries() -> List<ScheduleWitnessEntry> {
  fold(falsifier_rehomed_bin_wet_rows, init: [], f: fn(acc, r) {
    concat(acc, [bin_wet(entry: r.entry, f: r.function)])
  })
}

fn corpus_long(entry: String, f: String) -> ScheduleWitnessEntry {
  ScheduleWitnessEntry { entry: entry, function: f, kind: CorpusWitnessKind }
}

type SubstrateLongLaneRow {
  entry: String
  function: String
  reason: String
  dissolution: DissolutionCondition
}

data falsifier_substrate_long_lane_note: String = "Batch 6 (test-decomposition Class C, 2026-07-25): the declared Hermetic lane for SubstrateInputsOnly ingest/parse pipeline witnesses whose own eval exceeds the per-PR 5s fast-lane budget (gunbc_ci_fast_lane_rule_note) but are not wet integration — the live-grain half of the provenance-producer Class C split (fixture fail-closed walls stay per-PR via hand-built rows in affected_set_provenance_producer_test.dag and sg_claims_test.dag selectivity receipts). Its designed ordering (SelectionApplied after the rehomed-bin-wet batch, halted by claim_executor if an earlier batch fails) DESCRIBES the batch's place in a schedule, not a schedule that currently runs it.

CADENCE STANDING — RUNG DROP, DECLARED (effective 611fd02770/#8283, 2026-08-15; this note rewritten 2026-08-19, dashboard node adhoc-1eb1a9f9-ad9). PREVIOUS RUNG: every admitted long-lane identity (and, by the same falsifier.yml, every FalsifierRehomedBinWet and FalsifierSelfHostWet identity) had a scheduled route through the falsifier workflow — WitnessHasExecutingConsumer was a true claim for these cadences. CURRENT RUNG: falsifier.yml, the sole scheduled executor, was deleted at 611fd02770/#8283; the cadence is declared but unrealized, and every identity classified into it has no execution route and zero coverage. std.witness_admission witness_cadence_has_scheduled_route(FalsifierSubstrateLongLane) is false; witness_execution_standing_for_row now derives DeclaredCadenceUnrealized for these identities rather than WitnessHasExecutingConsumer. REASON: FLOOR-Y (the 2026-08-15 required-floor cut, #8283) deliberately deleted falsifier.yml along with ci.yml and falsifier-alert.yml and reserved re-adding a cadence executor for a separate, later operator agreement — restoring or improvising one here would be a new gate decision this note does not make. BOUNDED POPULATION: the exact identity union of every admission source whose cadence is FalsifierSubstrateLongLane — falsifier_substrate_long_lane_batch_schedule_entries() below, not a transcribed count (DESIGN §3 single authority: that function already computes this union via witness_long_eval_budget_union_in over falsifier_substrate_long_lane_entries() and explicit_witness_admission_substrate_long_lane_roster()). RESTORATION: an identity leaves this declared-unrealized state only when (a) a separately agreed realized consumer reaches it, (b) it returns to an already-realized per-PR route (DiscoverySelection etc.), (c) it moves to another genuinely realized consumer, or (d) the obligation deletes as duplicate or non-discriminating — deliberately NOT 'one future cron fixes all of them': the roster is heterogeneous (real breadth censuses, repeated interpreted pipelines, integration receipts, and likely some redundant rows), and root-cause work may dissolve much of it before any cadence executor is even reconsidered. THIS NOTE reveals and types an already-existing drop; it neither deletes an executor nor creates a coverage loss. Local recipe until a route exists: claim_batch --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry <file> --functions <csv>."

