  SubstrateLongLaneRow {
    entry: "src/v2/test/claim/long/realization_vocabulary_containment_witness_test.dag",
    function: "realization_vocab_live_corpus_receipt_holds",
    reason: "TS-0/LANG-2 live-corpus containment receipt: irreducible live-tree census over realization_vocab_consumer_scan_roots verifying every current leak edge is grandfathered and containment holds corpus-wide. Enrolled on the falsifier substrate long lane for its corpus/integration role — the observation that must read the live import graph — not because per-PR discovery is the right admission surface. Per-PR mechanism coverage stays in no_new_debt_gate_test.dag and the existing synthetic/scanner/roster-soundness receipts.",
    dissolution: unbound_dissolution(description: "replaced by a cheaper structural receipt proving the same live-corpus relation, or live containment observation becomes unnecessary")
  },
  SubstrateLongLaneRow {
    entry: "src/v2/test/claim/body_lowering/long/atom_body_discriminator_witness_test.dag",
    function: "atom_body_discriminator_single_pass_receipt_holds",
    reason: "~18661ms thread-CPU measured locally (2026-08-14; wall=18704ms) — 3.7× over the 5s fast-lane budget. The 5001ms figure is only where a --eval-budget-ms 5000 probe aborted (EvalBudgetExceeded), not completed witness cost. One tokenize→parse→normalize over the four-declaration atom-body discriminator module, then declaration/parameter_count/ArrowBodyForm production rows plus both RED mirror directions on the same normalized tree. The cost is the production frontend crossing — not a second pass and not a synthetic node_synthetic fixture.",
    dissolution: unbound_dissolution(description: "witness realization lands the frontend natively or eval drops under gunbc_ci_fast_lane_witness_eval_budget on a measured run — then re-enroll per-PR discovery and delete this row")
  }
]

fn falsifier_substrate_long_lane_entries() -> List<ScheduleWitnessEntry> {
  fold(falsifier_substrate_long_lane_rows, init: [], f: fn(acc, r) {
    concat(acc, [corpus_long(entry: r.entry, f: r.function)])
  })
}

data falsifier_substrate_long_lane_batch_schedule_note: String = "Batch 6 roster derivation: legacy falsifier_substrate_long_lane_rows plus explicit_witness_admission_substrate_long_lane_roster, identity-joined (witness_long_eval_budget_union_in) — this is the exact-identity bounded population falsifier_substrate_long_lane_note's CADENCE STANDING paragraph cites, not a currently-executing schedule (falsifier.yml, batch 6's sole invoker, was deleted at 611fd02770/#8283). Declared-long-budget admission rows join here without joining falsifier_substrate_long_lane_rows — falsifier_substrate_long_lane_entries stays the legacy roster only so declared_long_budget_reaches_the_ceiling_roster_without_the_batch_roster can refuse dual enrollment."

fn falsifier_substrate_long_lane_batch_schedule_entries() -> List<ScheduleWitnessEntry> {
  witness_long_eval_budget_union_in(
    batch: falsifier_substrate_long_lane_entries(),
    declared: explicit_witness_admission_substrate_long_lane_roster()
  )
}

data witness_long_eval_budget_entries_note: String = "THE SCHEDULER'S CEILING CONDITION, and it is deliberately NOT the long-lane batch roster. Two different questions were answered by one list until 2026-08-06: WHICH BATCH RUNS THIS (falsifier_substrate_long_lane_rows above, batch 6) and HOW MUCH EVAL TIME THIS WITNESS NEEDS. Because claim_executor armed the 180s ceiling only where a batch's explicit entries intersected the batch roster, the second answer could only be obtained by joining the first — so an expensive KNOWN-RED root had to occur twice in the schedule, once for its polarity and once for its budget, and the second occurrence sat on a batch that expects green and paged the operator for a witness that is red by design (gunbc#7737). This union is the separation: batch membership still routes execution, gunbc.explicit_witness_admission witness_long_eval_budget_roster sizes the ceiling from each row's OWN declared budget, and a witness needs no second batch to be given the time it requires. The residual — declared by neither — keeps the fast lane, so an undeclared lane reds loudly at 5s rather than running unbounded (DESIGN 5, the arm narrows). LANE GRANULARITY, AND WHY THE KNOWN-RED LANE IS NO LONGER WIDENED BY IT (operator ruling, 2026-08-06): claim_executor scopes a ceiling to a BATCH, so a mixed batch holding one declared-long row runs every sibling at the long ceiling. The first shape of this change disclosed that widening and kept it; the correction removes it where it was introduced, by partitioning the known-red probe lane into two budget-homogeneous batches derived from the declared budget (gunbc.explicit_witness_admission known_red_probe_budget_partition_note). Each batch therefore arms exactly the ceiling its own rows declared. The residual widening is the pre-existing substrate long-lane batch, unchanged by this lane and narrowing on the same trigger. IT IS AN IDENTITY SET, NOT A CONCATENATION (review, 2026-08-06): a witness reaching the ceiling through BOTH inputs — on the long-lane batch roster and also declaring SubstrateLongLaneEvalBudget on its admission row — is a legitimate and expected state during the migration, and a bare concat would list it twice. Membership joins on schedule_witness_entry_eq (entry, function, kind), the same identity grain the schedule-multiplicity wall uses, never a bare name. The fold is exposed as witness_long_eval_budget_union_in so a witness can plant the overlap the live inputs do not currently exhibit; a control that can only observe today's disjoint population proves nothing about the join. A duplicate here would not change which ceiling is armed, since the executor only asks whether the batch INTERSECTS this roster, but it would corrupt every count taken over it — including the witness that asserts a declared-budget row needs no second batch. Dissolve-on: per-witness declared cost envelopes replace the blanket lane ceiling, the same trigger long_lane_exclusion_note names; then this union collapses to the declared-budget roster alone and each row is bounded by its own declaration."

fn witness_long_eval_budget_union_in(
  batch: List<ScheduleWitnessEntry>,
  declared: List<ScheduleWitnessEntry>
) -> List<ScheduleWitnessEntry> {
  fold(declared, init: batch, f: fn(acc, w) {
    if schedule_witness_entry_roster_contains(xs: acc, w: w) { acc } else { concat(acc, [w]) }
  })
}

fn witness_long_eval_budget_entries() -> List<ScheduleWitnessEntry> {
  witness_long_eval_budget_union_in(
    batch: falsifier_substrate_long_lane_entries(),
    declared: witness_long_eval_budget_roster()
  )
}

data resolution_divergence_silent_pick_gate_retirement_receipt: String = "RETIREMENT (operator 2026-08-18, gentle-tern-815). WHAT THE GATE CLAIMED: closure-scoped resolution-divergence census plus join-filtered SILENT-PICK-GATE refusals on genuine silent picks (global_bare_lcp, global_bare_lcp_tie, fn_parent_first_hit). THE DEFECT IS PRECONDITION ORDER, NOT PERFORMANCE: the gate checked its cheap decidable precondition LAST — it performed a second strict whole-corpus resolve and only then asked whether parent-plan telemetry was captured. Had it asked whether capture was armed BEFORE acquiring anything, it would have refused in microseconds the day the floor cut landed, loudly and for free. That ordering defect would still be wrong if the resolve were fast; 526s and +2.66GB RSS are the symptom, not the cause. WHY CAPTURE NEVER ARMED (both halves independently fatal): claim_executor returns from run_required_floor before the --plan-entry branch; capture_begin lives only under plan_function == gunbc_falsifier_plan inside that branch; witnesses.yml invokes only --required-floor; and src/v2/workflow/ci_floor_plan.dag (gunbc_falsifier_plan entry) was deleted by the floor cut — so the global stayed None and every run paid the full resolve cost before the foregone parent plan telemetry was not captured refusal. ENROLLMENT HID THE DEFECT: expected-red held means merely not-Pass, so a row failing structurally was indistinguishable from a row failing for the reason it was enrolled for — hiding 43% of slow time for the entire life of the floor, not a small miss. Measured: 526.1s wall, 4.6x next module, +2.66GB RSS. DELETED end-to-end: witness, transport, resolution_divergence_census bin, walk_target_alias_plan bin and cli_run walk-target planner (same silent-pick investigation family; zero CI consumers), in-process builtin, cli_run census machinery, falsifier roster rows. PRESERVED: v1_rt silent-pick recording hooks (main.rs compile-path proxy). Silent-pick divergence detection is NOT covered by any enrolled witness today. REBUILD CONSTRAINT: do NOT substitute the calling witness InterpContext for a whole-corpus census subject — the floor evaluates each claim through claim_scope_for, which scopes to that module's transitive import closure, not the prepared subject; reusing _calling_ctx (the obvious cheap repair) would silently narrow coverage from the whole corpus to one witness closure, run fast, report plausible sites_checked, and cover almost nothing (empty-observation narrow: bottom-as-answer conflated with bottom-as-ignorance). A future census must take the prepared module list explicitly; terminal shape is a function over that list whose typed receipt a constant-time witness asserts — not a witness that acquires or inherits its subject at evaluation time."

data walk_plan_stage_control_fixture_exclusion_note: String = "test/fixture/walk_plan_stage/ is excluded from tree-wide discovery at DIR grain (the fixture-home ruling of 2026-07-11: a fixture that WANTS witness enrollment is mis-homed by definition, and file-grain exclusion invites the next control fixture to repeat the mistake): these are production-path stage-executor controls with Wet typed-service bodies (shell.Mkdir/Remove/Test, Filesystem.Read/Write, sleep.Delay) driven only through claim_executor --plan-entry/--plan-function recipes in plan.dag. As hermetic discovery witnesses they refuse at the effect boundary (no mock_response for Parents/Write/Read/RecursiveForce) or carry BY-DESIGN reds (failure_red_member_holds); inclusion turned every PR touching the import closure into 8 WitnessRed failures in discovery batch 3. Explicit plan-driven runs and walk_plan_stage_fixture.rs (#[ignore] integration) are unaffected."

data enforcement_coverage_exclusion_note: String = "The four enforcement inventory/coverage witnesses (enforcement/cost_coverage_witness_test.dag, enforcement/grammar_coverage_witness_test.dag, enforcement_live_witness_test.dag, enforcement_inventory_witness_test.dag) are operator-ruled OFFLINE (2026-07-11; enforcement_inventory_witness_test.dag added 2026-08-02 review 47569). Receipt: their *_live fns read the corpus as data (live-tree rosters), so the PR-A never-predict-skip rule for live-tree rows made them run on EVERY wide PR regardless of diff; the block cost 22.0 min (main run 29137081535, busy fleet) and 21.0 min (PR run 29142398465, quiet fleet) of the 60-minute floor budget - about 35 percent - and their allocation ramp feeds the ~15GiB slot memory.high throttle that turns the floor tail into swap-speed work. Their input is corpus-denominated (the InputEnvelope axis, not layer span): per-PR admission wants a declared bounded envelope, which these rows cannot declare today. Offlining required TWO edits (cursor review catch, same PR): the discovery exclusion rows here AND removing the explicit CommitCheckEnrollment for enforcement_live_witness_test.dag in gunbc.commit_workflow - explicit roster rows merge after discovery with no exclusion filter (cli_run.rs explicit_entries dedup), and that is correct: an explicitly declared row should run, so offlining one means deleting its declaration, never teaching exclusions to veto the roster (a second authority). Run them via the local recipe: claim_batch --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry <entry> per fn (all pure reads, no --wet needed). Dissolve-on: witness rows declare InputEnvelope/CostEnvelope and the scheduled (nightly) lane admits corpus-input rows under its own budget - then re-enroll consciously through the floor owner's lane; the affected-set-falsifier cadence covers interim drift."

data accumulator_copy_roster_gate_exclusion_note: String = "The three accumulator_copy_roster_gate*_test.dag witnesses are operator-ruled OFFLINE (2026-07-10: the gate is ~15m of serial interpreted resolve; run it via the claim_batch recipe in v2.lens.complexity_accumulator_copy.roster_gate). Excluded from discovery because the flip's selection cannot see them honestly either way: file_gate reads its roster targets via filesystem_read at runtime — a data dependency invisible to resolve-closure attribution — and the live-scan classifier reads only entry-file text, so the rows would be intermittently selected by lens/std-closure PRs (cost, against the ruling) while never firing on roster-target-only PRs (no enforcement). Dissolve-on: resolved-graph memoization receipts land AND G2 path-intersection (not G1 module-closure alone) is wired into floor admission axis (iv); then re-enroll consciously through the floor owner's lane."

data identity_captured_navigation_roster_gate_exclusion_note: String = "src/v2/test/claim/identity_captured_navigation/roster_gate_test.dag is operator-ruled OFFLINE for the identical structural reason as accumulator_copy_roster_gate_exclusion_note (2026-07-14): its corpus-sweep test fns call file_gate, which reads its roster targets (src/v2/extdeps/languages/dag.dag and siblings) via filesystem_read at runtime — a data dependency invisible to resolve-closure attribution — so per-PR selection would fire intermittently on lens/std-closure PRs (cost, against the ruling) while never firing on roster-target-only PRs (no enforcement). Run via the local recipe in v2.lens.identity_captured_navigation.roster_gate. Dissolve-on: identical to accumulator_copy_roster_gate — resolved-graph memoization receipts land AND G2 path-intersection is wired into floor admission axis (iv); then re-enroll consciously through the floor owner's lane."

data lever_a_local_receipt_witness_exclusion_note: String = "dag/test/claim/lever_a_local_receipt_witness_test.dag is operator-ruled OFFLINE (2026-07-11: witness_touched_path_dispositions_hold cold-scans compile_clean_shard_entry_paths via module_declaration_facts once per scoped disposition row — O(rows) full dag entry-tree walks, 85m+ CI timeout / OOM when selection runs it after lens_verdict on cli_run.dag PRs). LOCAL RECIPE (the whole of it — this row is the authority, no script file to maintain): claim_batch --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry dag/test/claim/lever_a_local_receipt_witness_test.dag --function lever_a_local_receipts_hold --claim-run --wet. It formerly lived in scripts/lever_a_local_verify.sh, a pure sequencer around exactly that argv, deleted 2026-07-23 with the rest of scripts/ (operator ruling: a recipe is a command, not a file). Excluded from discovery for the same structural reason as accumulator_copy_roster_gate: the scoped rows read the shard roster at runtime — invisible to import-closure attribution — so skip-before-resolve cannot honestly bound cost. Dissolve-on: single-roster memo in tools.dag_compile_clean_scope lands AND G2 path-intersection (not G1 module-closure alone) is wired into floor admission axis (iv); then re-enroll through the floor owner's lane."

data whole_tree_strict_resolve_scaffold_exclusion_note: String = "The per-file rows below (everything after the three blanket prefixes and the two lens/application rows) are the strict-resolve-broken set, baked as single authority per operator ruling 2026-07-13 ('just make it single authority') — previously re-derived per probe run as --exclude-subpath args (M0/M1a receipts, docs/plans/v1-run-stability-throughline.md), a parallel representation this bake dissolves. Audited file-by-file 2026-07-13 (24 files, 5-group sweep with per-file execution receipts): 7 genuinely dead scaffolds were DELETED with their rows (the four Wave-A rung evals, the A.1.5a inprocess_equivalence one-shot, manual_corpus_eval, lens/idempotency/subject_roster — none witness-enrolled, zero importers, absent from the 1,776-witness cold corpus run); every row remaining guards a LIVE file — floor-discovered witnesses or their roster/receipt/lens dependencies, proven green by execution (the lens/testgen/ trio's four test-data witnesses PASS in the cold corpus run, overturning an initial dead-scaffold read). Their strict-resolve reds are universe-relative artifacts, NOT tree rot: each imports modules that EXIST in-tree (v2.test.manual.eval_runtime, v2.test.manual.connective_anchors, test fixtures) but sit behind this list's own blanket '/test/' and 'test/fixture/' rows, so the probe universe drops the import target while keeping the importer. Consumers are probe/instrument/census class only (measure_whole_tree_resolve, capture_func_env_semantic_oracle, wiring_liveness_whole_tree, measure_dependency_view_build, fn_arrow_decl_substrate census) — no witness-discovery or CI-gate coverage narrows. Dissolve each row on: its file relocates under a /test/ path (leaving the probe universe together with its import targets) or the blanket /test/ exclusion policy changes so its resolve repairs; a row that excludes nothing is dead weight, delete it. First relocation receipt (2026-07-14): the spice pair (spice_rc_passive_deck_claims_test, spice_rc_ngspice_oracle_test) re-homed to src/v2/test/claim/extdeps/ — they leave the probe universe with their fixtures, stay witness-discovered, and their two rows deleted per this trigger."

